[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: scribe previews every writing verb

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-SCRIBE-DRY-RUN
TITLE: scribe previews every writing verb
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
scribe grows --dry-run on every writing verb: new (every type leaf), set,
relate, unrelate, move, delete. The flag is added once, by walking the built
subparsers for every name in scribe_protocol.WRITES, and folded into the RPC
payload once, not per verb. A dry run performs everything the real run does up
to the write: it applies the change in memory, runs the same prechecks, and
proves every touched document renders and reparses. Then it prints a unified
diff of what would be written, path by path, computed from Graph.pending()
against the file's current bytes, and writes nothing. An empty diff prints that
nothing would change. A change the real run would refuse is refused by the dry
run with the same message and exit code. For move, the dry run prints the rename
it would perform. A move preserves the file's bytes, but both its dry and real
paths render and reparse the source before the rename, so either refuses a
document that does not round-trip. After a dry run the daemon's next read is
identical to before it; how that is achieved (discard and reload, or mutate a
copy) is chosen by measurement and recorded on this node. The diff helper is
shared between scribe and sdoc_cli.py rather than copied. The sdoc skill and
docs/sdoc/README.md say the flag exists and what it prints.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Implemented 2026-09-03. The client walks the built parser leaves named by
scribe_protocol.WRITES, adds --dry-run in one place, and folds dry_run into
every write payload in one place. Both writer CLIs use scribe_diff.py for
byte-based, path-by-path unified diffs. Workspace.write runs the ordinary
mutation, precheck, render and reparse pipeline, captures Graph.pending(), then
discards the speculative generation instead of saving it. A separate
last-published counter survives that discard, so the next reload always advances
the generation used by the board cache.

A move preserves the source bytes and therefore previews only its rename. Both
the real and dry-run move paths explicitly touch, render and reparse the source
document before rename; this preserves validation parity and deliberately means
either path refuses a document that does not round-trip. Graph.touch_document is
the public mutation seam used for that validation.

The held-state choice was remeasured on 2026-09-04 on the tracked corpus after
making the generation counter monotonic. Across three isolated runs, capturing
and discarding a no-change preview averaged 6.3 ms (6.5, 6.1 and 6.3 ms), and
the next full read averaged 943.1 ms (955.1, 895.1 and 979.2 ms). The earlier
deepcopy measurement was 4,444.9 ms in one run, about 4.7 times the remeasured
discard/reload cost, so copying remains rejected. The focused suite count is
updated by the follow-up commits that complete the reviewed contracts.
<<<
